# Vercel Web Analytics Integration

Successfully configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project.

## What was implemented:

### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
Retrieved the most up-to-date installation instructions from the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart) to ensure correct implementation.

### 2. Identified Framework
Determined this is a React application using Vite as the build tool (not Next.js).

### 3. Package Installation
The `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) was already present in package.json dependencies. Ran `npm install` to ensure the lock file is up to date.

### 4. Added Analytics Component
Modified `/src/main.jsx` to render the Analytics component following the official React integration pattern:
- The Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/react` was already imported
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the render tree inside StrictMode
- This enables automatic page view tracking for the application

## Files Modified:
- `src/main.jsx` - Added Analytics component to the React render tree
- `package-lock.json` - Updated by npm install to ensure dependency consistency

## Implementation Details:
According to the official Vercel documentation for React applications, the Analytics component should be imported from `@vercel/analytics/react` and included in the main App component. Since this project uses `main.jsx` as the entry point, I added it there inside the StrictMode wrapper alongside the main App component.

## Verification:
✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ No new linting errors introduced
✅ Dependencies installed and lock file updated

## Next Steps for Deployment:
1. Enable Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics tab → Enable button)
2. Deploy the application using `vercel deploy`
3. After deployment, verify analytics tracking by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view`
4. View collected data in the Vercel dashboard's Analytics section

## Notes:
- Pre-existing linting error in `src/rwc (1).jsx` (unused variable 'BMatch') was not addressed as it's unrelated to this Analytics integration
- The Analytics component will automatically track page views once the app is deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration is required for basic page view tracking
